# Keep Python bytecode caches out of the build context. The overlay files are
# COPY'd verbatim into the image, so a stray __pycache__/ (e.g. a compiled
# safety_envelope.pyc or training_manager.pyc left over from a deleted source)
# must never enter the context — otherwise a local/dirty-tree build could ship
# bytecode for a file whose source no longer exists. CI refuses dirty trees, but
# this guarantees the same for ad-hoc local builds.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
